// From the law's drawing, Constitutional Law 8 of 1959: 1.20 m by 1.80 m, with the yellow
// band's edges 1.20 m and 1.80 m along the top from the hoist and 0.60 m along the bottom,
// so its edges are the lines x + y = 120 and x + y = 180. That makes the bars 120, 60, 120
// measured along the same diagonal, which is 2:1:2 at 45 degrees.
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Republic of the Congo"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20151117022520/http://cour-constitutionnelle.cg/constitutionsanterieures/Loiconstitutionnelle8.pdf"
  source "https://faolex.fao.org/docs/pdf/con183097.pdf"
  source "https://www.crwflags.com/fotw/flags/cg.html"
  note "The 1959 law was read in the Constitutional Court's copy, which cites the Journal officiel of 15 September 1959. The Constitution of 2015 keeps the description and leaves dimensions and shades to a law. No later law on them was found, so the 1959 law's drawing is the most recent construction read."
  note "No law read gives a shade. The hex, Pantone and CMYK values are the Album des Pavillons 2023's, as FOTW reports them."
  note "The 1959 law also puts a triangular spearhead on the staff, which this omits."
  law "Constitution of the Republic of the Congo, 25 October 2015, Article 3" {
    source "https://faolex.fao.org/docs/pdf/con183097.pdf"
  }
  law "Constitutional Law No. 8 of 18 August 1959 fixing the flag of the Republic of the Congo" {
    source "https://web.archive.org/web/20151117022520/http://cour-constitutionnelle.cg/constitutionsanterieures/Loiconstitutionnelle8.pdf"
  }
}
palette {
  green "#169b62" {
    pantone "347 C"
    cmyk 81 12 76 1
  }
  yellow "#fcd116" {
    pantone "115 C"
    cmyk 2 17 91 0
  }
  red "#da291c" {
    pantone "485 C"
    cmyk 6 94 96 0
  }
}
proportion hoist=120 fly=180

bars green yellow red {
  rotate -45
  ratio 2 1 2
}
